+/**
+ * One phone-time outing of hers on his screen, lent: one of his apps opened on his unlocked
+ * screen, and the loop of look → step call → parse → carry out the verb, until she is done or
+ * the screen is his again. It runs inside the host of her outings ([com.opendroid.ai.core.life.OutingHost]),
+ * which started it and which Stop cancels.
+ *
+ * - Each step is one call of hers ([Mind.step]): she is shown a fresh look at the screen, a
+ *   picture of the app's window through her eyes where they are open (her own sight where her
+ *   brain sees, the describer otherwise; a protected screen is said to be one), and its labels.
+ *   She answers with one `do:` of the closed set ([PhoneVerb]); the code's hands carry it out
+ *   ([PhoneSpace]), moving as she would ([HumanMotion]), only where the look-only guard lets them
+ *   ([LookOnly]).
+ * - It ends the instant he takes the screen back ([LendWatch]): a touch, a tap, the screen off or
+ *   locked, a call, a notification, another app; the job is cancelled at once, which cuts off any
+ *   touch in flight. Before each step the rules of §1.1 for a lent screen are asked: his talk,
+ *   her sleep, his switches, power, the ledger, three guard refusals end it. A screen that is his
+ *   to answer (a sign-in, a payment, a permission) ends it too.
+ * - When it ends, the screen is given back as it was (home, or his app), whenever her app was
+ *   launched, however it ended: after a call only once the call is over; where a move of hers
+ *   took the app away (a link to another app, a back out of it, a sign-in her tap opened) his
+ *   screen is put back all the same. What she started playing is paused, then his sound is put
+ *   back. On his yes in the shade, the shade is closed first.
+ * - Her log ([HerLog]) gets counts, what she opened by
+ *   its label and her search words, never what she thought or what the screen showed (I8). The
+ *   phone's record gets the outing as hers in his app ([OutingEntries.phoneTime]).
+ */
+class PhoneOuting(
