+ * kept as he gave it: the same bytes, never decoded and written again, never scaled. So are
+ * the pictures that come with the app ([HerRefs], put in on the first start of a build) and
+ * the reference sheets ([addSheet]), which may become masters. A picture she made is derived
+ * and is kept as a JPEG no larger than [PersonaPictureRules.MAX_SIDE], as is the background
+ * picture. What goes out with a request is made from the kept file in memory and never
+ * written back: a JPEG of that size for her model to see ([base64]), and for an image model
+ * to work from the picture as it is in the file, without the file's metadata, where the request
+ * can carry it, else a copy no larger than [MAX_SOURCE_SIDE] ([source]), and only of an
+ * original or a master.
+ *
+ * All file work happens off the main thread, one change at a time. A damaged index or
+ * a missing file costs that entry in the list and nothing else: a picture file is only
+ * ever deleted because the owner removed or replaced that picture, or says so himself
+ * ([removeUnlisted]).
